# purpose
Purchases are approved in chat, and large ones slip through without a director.
purchases approved by the right person, up
Every purchase is approved by the right person. Large ones go to a director.
# people and things
staff: raise and submit purchase requests; team lead: approves or rejects purchase requests; director: approves large purchases
Purchase request: something the team wants to buy | amount: number, items: integer
# an example, then the actions in your words
PR-4: amount 1800, items 3
raise_purchase: Raise a purchase request -> new Purchase request; submit_purchase: Submit the request -> Purchase request; approve_purchase: Approve the request -> Purchase request; reject_purchase: Reject the request -> Purchase request
# who may (four actions), the limit, who must not: the recommended choices
 
 
 
 
 
 
# stages, then each action's column and the outcome rule: recommended
status: draft, submitted, approved, rejected; starts draft
 
 
 
 
# invariants: nothing beyond the stages
nothing
# world
staff: sam; team lead: tia; director: dora
staff raise_purchase P-1 amount=3000 items=2 -> draft; staff submit_purchase P-1 -> submitted; team_lead approve_purchase P-1 -> refused limit-amount; director approve_purchase P-1 -> approved
# handoffs: none
none
# review: confirm
yes
